Description: pco: lower 8-bit and 16-bit integers and memory accesses to 32 bit
 The backend only allocates 32-bit registers (pco_ra.c asserts only_32bit),
 the buffer, push constant, shared memory and scratch paths in
 pco_trans_nir.c only handle 32-bit data, and byte offsets of push constants
 and shared memory become dword offsets in pco_nir_lower_io(). Integer
 conversions to and from 16 bit were plain moves.
 .
 Memory accesses of UBOs, SSBOs, push constants, shared memory and scratch
 are split into dword-aligned 32-bit accesses with
 nir_lower_mem_access_bit_sizes() after the robustness lowering, so bounds
 checks still see the original access. Partial dword stores become a pair of
 32-bit atomic and/or operations (SSBO, shared) or a read-modify-write
 (scratch), so neighbouring bytes written by other invocations are kept.
 32-bit accesses that are already aligned are left unchanged.
 .
 ALU operations and subgroup operations on 8-bit and 16-bit values are
 widened with nir_lower_bit_size() before pco_nir_lower_subgroups(), after
 the memory lowering and at the end of pco_postprocess_nir(). Only moves,
 vectors, phis and conversions reach the backend at small bit sizes; they are
 held in 32-bit registers whose upper bits are undefined. Widening
 conversions now zero- or sign-extend with ubfe/ibfe, narrowing conversions
 stay moves, conversions from float16 and to float16 go through float32,
 and pack_32_2x16_split and unpack_32_2x16_split_x/y are lowered by
 nir_opt_algebraic. The shared memory size is aligned to a dword, since the
 coefficient allocation in pvr_alloc_cs_shmem() rounds it down.
 .
 No device feature changes here.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
